title: 'statement gossip: bound outbound sends with a per-peer outbox'
doc:
- audience: Node Operator
  description: |-
    The statement gossip protocol encoded every propagation chunk for every peer
    up front, holding an unbounded number of encoded payloads for up to ten
    seconds each when peers read slowly. Propagation now queues hashes to a
    per-peer outbox (at most 64 Ki hashes, 2 MiB, oldest dropped first and
    counted by the `outbox_full` reason of
    `substrate_sync_statement_undelivered_total`), keeps at most one chunk per
    peer in flight, and encodes statements from the store only when the peer's
    send slot is free. Initial-sync chunks share the propagation fetch path and
    now also skip statements the receiving peer itself sent us. Initial-sync
    and propagation chunks together are capped at 16 MiB in flight, observable
    via the new `substrate_sync_propagation_in_flight_bytes` gauge next to the
    existing initial-sync one.
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    `MAX_INITIAL_SYNC_IN_FLIGHT_BYTES` in `sc_network_statement::config` is
    renamed to `MAX_SEND_IN_FLIGHT_BYTES` and now covers propagation and
    initial-sync chunks together. `MAX_PROPAGATION_OUTBOX_LEN` is added.
crates:
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: major
